Z||000000||Matthew_Fiero||08-30-2001||01:12 AM||||I have done many searches and cannot find a problem quite like mine, keep in mind the car is constantly stationary during these tests (The car is unplated)<BR>I have an 85 GT 4psd. When the car is NOT running, i press the clutch down and shift into all gears, i can get it into reverse, 1st and 2nd, i cannot get it into 3rd or 4th. <BR>When the car is RUNNING, i try to shift it into reverse, and all it does is do an extreamly loud grinding noise, and it shifts into 1st and second no problem. But i stillcan't get it into 3rd or 4th.  I can also shift into 1st and 2nd if i am not pressing on the clutch, and if the car is off i can go into reverse without pressing clutch. What is my problem here? I have been told that i may need a new clutch. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Matthew_Fiero||08-30-2001||10:25 AM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||08-30-2001||10:39 AM||||I'm by no means an expert.  I'll assume you've read all you can about our clutches (Archies site, fiero secrets site, etc).<P>Have you had someone shift while you check the mechanical end of things?  Broken brackets, binding shift cables, poorly adjusted cables, insufficient travel at the slave and others can affect the shifting.<P>Good luck!<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000003||dman||08-30-2001||04:00 PM||||Hello everyone.<P>Since it engages and disengages fine when shifting into 1st and 2nd (while engine is running) I'd say the clutch is probably fine.<P>Since you can't get it into 3rd/4th and reverse I'd say try adjusting your select cable. Simple and free. Use deductive reasoning when diagnosing any mechanical problem.<P>If you don't already have one purchase a service manual. I believe both the Chilton's and Haynes manual should cover how you adjust the shift and select cables.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||08-30-2001||04:21 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013171.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013171.html</A> <BR>from a couple of days ago.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||08-30-2001||04:33 PM||||I'd say that the clutch isn't disengaging properly. Gears 1-2 should line up, so with the engine off, they'll go back and forth. 3-4 may not line up, and won't go 'cos you're pushing against the stopped motor, via clutch. With motor running, slap into 4th, and cut engine. Bet you'll be able to go 3-4 no problem, until you jam it in 1st. The fact that it grinds in reverse tells me the clutch ain't disengaging. Also, your shift cables might be out of adjustment, and that won't help things.||||reg||7
Z||000006||Matthew_Fiero||08-31-2001||01:50 AM||||dammit<BR>last night i blead the clutch to see if that would work, but now when the engine is running i cannot shift into any gear, and when i try to go into reverse it does the grinding sound still<BR>when car is off it still goes into reverse, 1st and 2nd<BR>did i blead it correctly?||||reg||1
